  "authorNotes": "Nursery Bangla. No Mohammadpur 2026 final exists for Nursery, so the guide is the Mohammadpur Annual 2025 Nursery Bangla paper (all MP items are MP_OTHER / MP_OTHER_ADAPTED). Its rows line up closely with the Sylhet syllabus and its content comes straight from the 2026 Nursery Bangla book (e.g. the word-matching set is book p.72, the jumbled sets are from book pp.18 and 75), so most of it was reused. Changes: Q1 Mohammadpur asked only ক–ন; the Sylhet row asks the whole alphabet, so it is split into 4 parts (vowels 4, ক–ণ 4, ত–ল 4, শ–ঁ 3 = 15). Q2 had 6 blanks in Mohammadpur; cut to 5. Q3/Q4 Mohammadpur had one jumbled set each; the other 4 sets in each are new, using the same letter groups as the book but jumbled differently. Q6 Mohammadpur had 9 items; one new item added (হ → ড়). Q9 Mohammadpur had 6 pairs; কলস was dropped to make 5. Q7 item 5: the Mohammadpur picture looks like a lotus, but the book's শ word is শাপলা, so the Office should use a clear water-lily picture. Things to check: (a) Q8 uses the book's letter pictures where the letter is not the first sound (ব্যাঙ → ঙ, চিংড়ি → ং, দুঃখী → ঃ, গাড়ি → গ) — this is exactly what Mohammadpur did and what the book teaches, but the reviewer may want to confirm. (b) Oral: the 10 marks are split across 7 prompts (2+2+2+1+1+1+1); '১২ মাসের নাম' was taken as the Bangla months. (c) Duration 1 h 30 min is copied from the Mohammadpur paper; the Sylhet time was not given. (d) Mohammadpur also had dictation (10) and cleanliness/class-work (4); the Sylhet syllabus has no such rows, so they are left out. Page numbers in bookRef are the printed page numbers of the 2026 Nursery Bangla book."
}
